export const FACTS = "Aside is a free, open-source Chrome extension that opens an AI sidebar on any webpage. It reads the page you are on, so you can summarize, translate, extract data or chat about it with Claude, OpenAI GPT, Gemini, Grok, Groq or a local Ollama model, without copy-pasting or leaving the tab. It is bring-your-own-key (BYOK): you add your own API key, it stays in your browser, and every request goes straight to the provider you chose. The interface is available in English and in Hebrew with full right-to-left (RTL) support.\nAside is 100% client-side. API keys live in chrome.storage.local - on your device only, never synced or uploaded anywhere. Requests go directly from your browser to the provider you chose. No telemetry, no analytics, no server in the middle.\nQ: Is Aside free? A: The extension is free and open source. You pay each AI provider directly for usage (or use a free tier - Groq and Gemini both offer one).\nQ: Where are my API keys stored? A: In chrome.storage.local - on your device only. They are never synced, uploaded, or sent to any server (the extension has no server at all). Conversation history is stored locally only, too.\nQ: Can I choose which model each provider uses? A: Yes. Each provider ships with a sensible default, and you can switch model right from the composer (or in Settings → Model), e.g. Claude Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5, or Haiku 5.5. There's also a Custom field to type any model id the provider supports, so you're never stuck waiting for us to add a new one. Custom ids are saved per provider, so they reappear under Saved custom for one-click reuse.\nQ: Which providers are supported? A: Anthropic Claude, OpenAI ChatGPT, Google Gemini, xAI Grok, Groq, and self-hosted Ollama. Adding more is straightforward - see the repo.\nQ: Which languages does it support? A: The interface ships in English and Hebrew with full right-to-left (RTL) support, and the sidebar follows the direction of RTL pages such as Hebrew or Arabic sites. The model can reply in any of eight languages: English, Hebrew, Spanish, French, German, Chinese, Arabic, and Japanese. On Auto it replies in the language of the page.\nQ: Can I run it on Firefox or Edge? A: Edge yes (Chromium-based). Firefox isn't packaged yet - contributions welcome.\nQ: Does it work with my ChatGPT Plus or Claude Pro subscription? A: No. Aside is bring-your-own-key (BYOK): it calls each provider's API with an API key you create in that provider's console, and API usage is billed separately from chat subscriptions. Groq and Gemini offer free API tiers, and a local Ollama model needs no key at all.\nQ: Is Aside on the Chrome Web Store? How do I install it? A: Not yet. Download aside.zip from the latest GitHub release, unzip it, open chrome://extensions, turn on Developer mode and click Load unpacked. It takes about 30 seconds, with no build step and no account.\nQ: What does Aside send, and to whom? A: Only what you ask for. When you send a prompt, Aside adds the readable text of the current page (trimmed to 12,000 characters) to that one request and sends it straight from your browser to the provider you picked. You can switch page context off with one click. Nothing is uploaded in the background, and there is no analytics or telemetry.";
